# Bildrath Cantemir, Bildrath's Mercantile (docs/voice/bildrath.md)
# Buying and selling are lines plus give/take/gold until the merchant screen exists. Prices are ten times the PHB.

~ start
if flag.bildrath_banned and not flag.bildrath_repaid
-> banned
endif
if flag.bildrath_robbed and not flag.bildrath_accused
-> robbed
endif
if flag.bildrath_met
Bildrath: Back again. The prices haven't changed. They never change. That's what makes them prices.
-> menu
endif
set bildrath_met
Narrator: Everything in the shop is dusted, labeled and squared to the edge of its shelf. Behind the counter, a narrow man in a spotless apron is already reaching for a pencil.
Bildrath: Welcome to Bildrath's Mercantile. Prices are posted. They are ten times what you're used to. You are used to the wrong place.
interject background:criminal: What a lovely, sturdy counter. Very... sturdy.
-> menu

~ menu
* Show us what you have. -> buy
* We have things to sell. -> sell
* [if not flag.bildrath_discount and not flag.bildrath_haggle_failed] Surely we can come to a better arrangement. -> haggle
* Any news in the village? -> news
* [if flag.burial_agreed and not flag.parriwimple_pallbearer and not flag.burgomaster_buried] We need help carrying a coffin. -> hire
* Goodbye. -> END

~ buy
if flag.bildrath_discount
Bildrath [weary]: For you, the special price. Nine times. I'll never recover. Rope ten, torches one for five, rations five a day, oil one a flask. Healer's kit forty-five. The potion, four hundred and fifty.
else
Bildrath: Rope, ten gold. Torches, one gold for five. Rations, five gold a day. Lamp oil, one gold a flask. A healer's kit, fifty. And the potion in the case, five hundred.
endif
interject class:rogue: That much? For one potion? I've stolen less. In theory. Hypothetically. Never mind.
* Fifty feet of rope. (10 gp) -> buy_rope
* Five torches. (1 gp) -> buy_torches
* Three days of rations. (15 gp) -> buy_rations
* A flask of oil. (1 gp) -> buy_oil
* [if not flag.bildrath_discount] A healer's kit. (50 gp) -> buy_kit
* [if flag.bildrath_discount] A healer's kit. (45 gp) -> buy_kit_discount
* [if not flag.bildrath_discount and not flag.bildrath_potion_sold] The potion. (500 gp) -> buy_potion
* [if flag.bildrath_discount and not flag.bildrath_potion_sold] The potion. (450 gp) -> buy_potion_discount
* That's all. -> menu

~ buy_rope
gold -10
give rope 1
Bildrath: Ten gold. Hempen, fifty feet, guaranteed to hold anything you can afford to hang from it.
-> buy

~ buy_torches
gold -1
give torch 5
Bildrath: One gold. They burn an hour apiece, which is more than most things here manage.
-> buy

~ buy_rations
gold -15
give ration 3
Bildrath: Fifteen gold. Hard bread, harder cheese, and a sausage of no fixed species.
-> buy

~ buy_oil
gold -1
give oil 1
Bildrath: One gold. Lamp oil. Also burns other things, which I mention for no reason at all.
-> buy

~ buy_kit
gold -50
give healers_kit 1
Bildrath: Fifty gold. Bandages, splints, salve. The burgomaster used one up in a month, before the end.
-> buy

~ buy_kit_discount
gold -45
give healers_kit 1
Bildrath [weary]: Forty-five. I want you to know this hurts me more than it hurts you.
-> buy

~ buy_potion
gold -500
give potion_of_healing 1
set bildrath_potion_sold
Bildrath [smile]: Five hundred gold. In twenty years nobody has bought it. I'd come to think of it as family. Goodbye, little bottle.
-> buy

~ buy_potion_discount
gold -450
give potion_of_healing 1
set bildrath_potion_sold
Bildrath [weary]: Four hundred and fifty. Take it before I change my mind. Take it. Go on.
-> buy

~ sell
Bildrath: I pay a tenth of what a thing is worth. That is not greed; that is arithmetic. Everyone in this valley already owns a sword, and none of them helped.
* [if item:shortsword] Sell a shortsword. (1 gp) -> sell_shortsword
* [if item:longsword] Sell a longsword. (1 gp) -> sell_longsword
* [if item:shield] Sell a shield. (1 gp) -> sell_shield
* [if item:chain_mail] Sell a coat of chain mail. (7 gp) -> sell_chain
* Never mind. -> menu

~ sell_shortsword
take shortsword 1
gold +1
Bildrath: One gold. I'll put it with the others.
-> sell

~ sell_longsword
take longsword 1
gold +1
Bildrath: One gold, and that's generous. It has a nick in it. Everything does, here.
-> sell

~ sell_shield
take shield 1
gold +1
Bildrath: One gold. Somebody will want to hide behind it. Everybody does, eventually.
-> sell

~ sell_chain
take chain_mail 1
gold +7
Bildrath: Seven gold. Heavy. I'll have Parriwimple carry it. I'll have Parriwimple carry everything.
-> sell

~ haggle
Bildrath: Haggling is a form of theft that takes longer.
* [Persuasion DC 18] A loyal customer is worth more than one sale. (one try) -> haggle_ok | haggle_fail
* [Intimidation DC 18] Lower the prices. (one try) -> haggle_ok | haggle_fail
* Never mind. -> menu

~ haggle_ok
set bildrath_discount
Bildrath [angry]: Ten percent. Ten! You have robbed me in broad daylight, and I let you. Parriwimple, write it down. No. Don't. I don't want a record of this.
Narrator: For all his outrage, he looks at you with something new: respect, the kind one shark has for another.
-> menu

~ haggle_fail
set bildrath_haggle_failed
Bildrath: No. The prices are posted. They will stay posted. You may look at them as long as you like; looking is free, for now.
-> menu

~ news
Bildrath: News costs nothing, which is what it's worth. Ask.
* The old woman with the pastry cart. -> news_morgantha
* Ismark. -> news_ismark
* The church. -> news_church
* The woman weeping down the lane. -> news_mary
* Enough news. -> menu

~ news_morgantha
Bildrath: Morgantha. Comes through every few weeks with that cart. I don't sell pastries; I have standards. Folk who can't pay her settle up some other way. I don't ask how. I don't give credit, and I suspect neither does she.
-> news

~ news_ismark
Bildrath: Ismark Kolyanovich owes this shop eleven gold and four silver. I mention it only because you appear to be his friends.
-> news

~ news_church
Bildrath: Father Donavich stopped buying candles. A priest who prays in the dark is either very holy or very ashamed. I don't extend credit to either.
-> news

~ news_mary
Bildrath: Mary bought three locks from me this year. Good locks. Her daughter went out of the window. You can't sell a lock for a window. Believe me, I've tried.
-> news

~ hire
Bildrath: Parriwimple's time is five gold an hour. A coffin takes an hour. A grave takes two. Fifteen gold, and he brings his own shovel, which is also mine.
* Fifteen gold. Done. (15 gp) -> hire_paid
* [if flag.parriwimple_befriended] Parriwimple already offered. For free. -> hire_free
* Too dear. -> menu

~ hire_paid
gold -15
set parriwimple_pallbearer
Bildrath: Parriwimple! The customers have purchased three hours of you. Take the good shovel. Bring it back clean.
Parriwimple [smile]: I can carry that.
-> menu

~ hire_free
set parriwimple_pallbearer
Bildrath [angry]: He offered. For free. Parriwimple, we will be having a talk about the concept of value. Go, then. Go! Bring the shovel back clean.
-> menu

~ robbed
set bildrath_accused
Bildrath [angry]: My strongbox is thirty gold lighter than it ought to be, and you are the only new faces in the valley. Parriwimple! Stand by the door.
* [Deception DC 15] We've no idea what you're talking about. (If he doesn't believe you, you're thrown out.) -> lie_ok | lie_fail
* Fine. Here's your money back. (30 gp) -> repay
* [Intimidation DC 14] Call your nephew off, or else. (If he doesn't back down, you're thrown out.) -> threat_ok | threat_fail

~ lie_ok
attitude bildrath indifferent
Bildrath: Hm. Perhaps. Perhaps it was the wolves. I shall be counting the spoons when you leave.
-> menu

~ lie_fail
set bildrath_banned
attitude bildrath hostile
Bildrath [angry]: You have coin in your purse that has my thumbprint on it. Out. Come back with thirty gold and an apology, in that order, or don't come back.
-> END

~ repay
gold -30
set bildrath_repaid
Bildrath: Thirty gold. I'll note that you returned it. I'll also note that you took it. My ledger has two columns for a reason.
-> menu

~ threat_ok
attitude bildrath hostile
Bildrath [afraid]: Parriwimple, sit down. Sit. They're... customers. Valued customers. Buy something, and then leave.
-> menu

~ threat_fail
set bildrath_banned
attitude bildrath hostile
Narrator: Parriwimple steps between you and his uncle, very gently, like a wall that has decided to be polite.
Bildrath: Out. Thieves aren't customers. They're weather.
-> END

~ banned
Bildrath [angry]: No. Out. You know the price of coming back in.
* Thirty gold, and an apology. We're sorry. (30 gp) -> unban
* We'll go. -> END

~ unban
gold -30
set bildrath_repaid
attitude bildrath indifferent
Bildrath: Thirty gold, and an apology. The gold, I accept. The apology I'll take under advisement. Browse. Touch nothing you haven't paid for.
-> menu
